<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle up $1 at $113/dressed - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle up $1 at $113/dressed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Steers and heifers were steady to $1.00 per cwt higher on a dressed basis delivered (paid on hot carcass weights), USDA said.</p>
<p>Dressed Basis Steers - Select and Choice 2-3 1200-1300 lbs 111.00- 113,00.  Dressed Basis Heifers - Select and Choice 2-3 1100-1225 lbs 111.00- 113.00.</p>
<p>Slaughter steers and heifers were not tested on a live basis, USDA said. Buyer inquiry good. Seller interest fair.</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers -  No confirmed sales.</p>
<p>Slaughter Heifers - No confirmed sales.</p>
<p>Confirmed - 3,200   For the week - 33,400</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720</p>
</text>
